-- title:
--   Archimedean local bridge in degree one at a complex place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a representation $M$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over $\mathbb Z/p$, where $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Let $F \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field that is a number field, Galois over $\mathbb Q$ and totally complex, let $w$ be an infinite place of $F$, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$. Let $\pi_i$ be a group homomorphism from `archimedeanDecomposition`, the subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ generated by the integral powers of [`complexConjugation`](def/GaloisRep_ComplexConjugation.html#L30) (the restriction to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of complex conjugation on $\mathbb C$), to the stabiliser $D_w$ of $w$ in $\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)$, assumed to satisfy $\pi_i(h) = \mathrm{res}_F(\sigma^{-1} h \sigma)$ for all $h$ and to be bijective, and assume $\sigma^{-1} c \sigma$ does not fix $F$ pointwise, $c$ denoting [`complexConjugation`](def/GaloisRep_ComplexConjugation.html#L30). Let $R \xrightarrow{f} P \xrightarrow{g} B$ be morphisms of representations of $\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)$ over $\mathbb Z$ with $f$ injective, $f,g$ exact and $g$ surjective, let $\alpha$ be a finite type with an isomorphism $P \cong \mathbb Z[\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)]^{(\alpha)}$, and suppose $p$ annihilates $B$. Let $\kappa$ be a biadditive pairing $B \times M \to (F_w)^\times$, written additively, which is equivariant in the sense that $\kappa(\rho_B(\pi_i h)b, \rho_M(h)m) = \pi_i(h) \cdot \kappa(b,m)$ for the action of $D_w$ on the units of the completion $F_w$, and perfect in the sense that every additive map $B \to (F_w)^\times$ is $\kappa(\cdot\,, m)$ for a unique $m \in M$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an additive homomorphism $\Lambda$ from the group of morphisms of $D_w$-representations from $R$ (restricted along the inclusion $D_w \hookrightarrow \mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)$) to $(F_w)^\times$, to $H^1$ of $M$ restricted along `archimedeanLoc`, such that: the predicate `IsLocalBridge₁` holds for $\pi_i$, the restrictions of $f$ and $g$, the target $(F_w)^\times$ restricted along $\pi_i$ with $\iota$ the identity, $\kappa$ and $\Lambda$; $\Lambda \varphi = 0$ precisely when $\varphi$ factors as the restriction of $f$ followed by some $\chi : P \to (F_w)^\times$ of $D_w$-representations; every value $\Lambda \varphi$ lies in `continuousH1 archimedeanLoc`, the image in $H^1$ under the cocycle-to-cohomology map of the submodule `levelCocycles₁`; and every element of that submodule is a value of $\Lambda$.
--
--   This is the archimedean term of the local duality computation at a complex place of the level, in the form $\mathrm{Ext}^1_{D_w}(-, F_w^\times) \cong H^1(\mathrm{Gal}(\mathbb C/\mathbb R), M)$, packaged as a bridge map $\Lambda$ with prescribed kernel and image. It specialises the abstract local-bridge construction of [`groupCohomology.exists_isLocalBridge1`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_isLocalBridge1) and its companions to the decomposition group at $w$, and feeds the assembly of the global duality statements [`groupCohomology.exists_mem_continuousH1S_locRes_eq_of_forall_sum_theta_eq_zero_arch_of_ne_two`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_mem_continuousH1S_locRes_eq_of_forall_sum_theta_eq_zero_arch_of_ne_two) and [`groupCohomology.exists_sha1_dualTwist_sha2_pairing_nondegenerate_of_ne_two`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_sha1_dualTwist_sha2_pairing_nondegenerate_of_ne_two).
